    info:'<b>Chromatin = DNA + histones + RNA + non-histone proteins.</b> Eukaryotes wrap DNA around histone octamers (~147 bp/nucleosome).<br><b>Two states:</b><br>• <b>Euchromatin</b>: open, transcribed. Hyperacetylated histones (HATs add Ac → neutralize + charge → loosen).<br>• <b>Heterochromatin</b>: closed, silenced. Deacetylated (HDACs) + methylated DNA + H3K9me3.<br><b>Modifications:</b><br>• <b>DNA methylation</b>: 5-mC at CpG islands → silencing. Maintained by DNMT1 through cell division.<br>• <b>Histone acetylation</b>: activating.<br>• <b>Histone methylation</b>: site-dependent (H3K4me3 = active, H3K27me3 = silencing).<br><b>Chromatin remodelers</b> (SWI/SNF) use ATP to slide nucleosomes.',
